5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T16:27:12-07:00","id":183317,"title":"","content":"I was thinking a goremaul as a sort of club. Is there an artifact version of a staff somewhere? I think I remember seeing a wrackstaff in one of the splats, looked similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","name":"4uk4ata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T19:52:27-07:00","id":183439,"title":"","content":"Checking in. I've been hit with the busy stick and it's been taking a while for me to finish writing my character. But I'll have it down in a couple of days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T05:02:05-07:00","id":183708,"title":"","content":"There is such a thing as a Wrackstaff, I'm not sure where to find 2.5 stats for it though.<br /> <br /> Based on comparing the stats of a Staff, Straight Sword and Daiklave, how about this?<br /> <br /> Wrackstaff: Speed 5, Accuracy +2, Damage 7B/2, Defense +2, Rate 3, Tags: 2, M, R, O. Same attunement cost as a Daiklave.<br /> <br /> A wrackstaff can have up to two hearthstone sockets, but some don't have any.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2082-schleiermacher","name":"Schleiermacher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T13:56:27-07:00","id":184061,"title":"","content":"I suppose this is a two-dot artefact? Normally I'd lean towards a club-like weapon, but that would mean picking melee or something like Earth Dragon, and I'm not sure I want to do that. BTW, I am working on a short backstory and wondering how to tie it in my abilities - what language do they speak in the Northwestern port cities, Seatongue, Low Realm or something else?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Story \u2013 in one of the windy ports of the Northwest there once was a boy called Federiko. At first he was little different than most of his peers, like most of the children there he sought excitement and wonder for his little world. In Port Cabrast, there were not that many forms of excitement, but he tried every one and wanted to invent a few more \u2013 new games, new tricks and, as he grew, new affairs. Yet of all those, his favourite excitement was to be surrounded by a garrulous group in the warm room of the tavern as tales were told of strange lands and great deeds as the wind blew outside, its icy teeth held at bay by the thick door but his howl adding to the charm of the tale. He himself was not the greatest of storytellers \u2013 though he was far from incapable \u2013 but an avid peruser. He eventually apprenticed himself in one of the small, dimly lit taverns where he served as a waiter, barkeep and at times bouncer, and in those dark evenings, he found his second passion \u2013 people. They all had stories in which they were the heroes, the villains, the distressed ones or even the onlookers, and each tale fascinated him. Some were simple, some were exotic, but each was a new world. In time, he sought to tug at the strings of those tales \u2013 prompting the protagonist to try this, say that, and hopefully get the story set to its proper path. To his credit, he found himself often succeeding, though he soon found out success wasn\u2019t always what he imagined it to be. Well, he thought, gods willing he would have a lifetime to improve. Something inside him wanted to set things right, as if perceiving the wrongness of the tales as a jarring note.<br /> Then, fate happened, and his little world was taken away from him, substituted by the promise to ply his talents on a scene unimaginably greater. He was thrilled by the opportunity at first, although he quickly became somewhat jaded with the factional baggage and hierarchy he found, in particular in the department he was assigned for, which he quickly coined several new nicknames for. On the other hand, the work he was provided with was occasionally quite enjoyable, and he found the days spent behind the huge bars at the Cerulean Lute to be fascinating beyond compare \u2013 and yet, somehow familiar. There is a sweet irony at learning how the spirit to which down-on-their-luck sailors back home is itself having a hard year, and it sometimes takes all his self-control to skew his smile into an understanding grimace. He has also made a couple of friends in Yu-Shan and back on Creation, and overall, considers his life a rather well enjoyed one. Getting his own landship, which he partly converted into an impromptu bar, is probably his greatest joy, and it is one of the reasons he so much likes spending time back in creation. He has so far avoided joining any of the major fractions at his time, preferring to keep his options open and focus on the work itself. It has not helped his career much, but he sees no reason to hurry.<br /> <br /> Federiko is now the man everyone instinctively calls barkeep. He is a large, fairly calm man (well-groomed moustache) in well-made clothes, moving around with a practiced and subdued grace. He favors white and dark grey or black, but always with some blue accessory. After all, one should respect one's trade.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3332,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","user":"4uk4ata","date":". 06-29-2014, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","name":"4uk4ata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T02:41:05-07:00","id":184678,"title":"","content":"Seatongue, Airtongue and/or Low Realm, it varies from place to place and many places probably use more than one language. And yes, two dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2082-schleiermacher","name":"Schleiermacher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T08:36:10-07:00","id":184851,"title":"","content":"Here's Wei's full character sheet. Let me know if you have questions or complaints.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Name: Lucky Wei</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Concept: Wandering Folk Hero</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Caste: Journeys</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Motivation</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: To inspire legends that encourage mortals to be adventurous. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Intimacies</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Tall tales (Passion), Allies (Friendship), Mercury (Respect), Golden Barque (Lazy Affection), Traveling (</span></span></span>Calling)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">ATTRIBUTES