/span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Essence: ***</span></span></span></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Health Levels</span></b></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">1x -0 </span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">2x -1</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">2x -2</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">1x -4</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Incap</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">2 Dying</span></span></span></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Backgrounds</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Allies *****: </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">1. Stone Bones - earth elemental or godblood - supremely strong. Able to lift, carry, and throw ridiculously large objects.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">2. Nimble Nayin - air elemental or godblood - supremely fast. Swift as sorcery.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">3. Glut - fire elemental or godblood - supreme eater. Can eat almost anything, no matter the volume. Can consume a whole herd of oxen without being full.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">4. Dolphin Scales - water elemental or godblood - supreme swimmer. holds breath indefinitely, commands small waves.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">5. Flower of the Mountains - wood nymph - supremely beautiful - has abilities that compel people to fawn over her and can exude a pollen that encourages feelings of love</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Contacts *****:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">1. King Raul of Rolston - Leader of a major state in the Scavenger Lands, owes Wei a favor for saving his kingdom (and not marrying his daughter afterwards). Links to eastern nobility.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">2. Zephyr Bringing Favorable Signs - Air elemental in a Western spirit court. Links to air elementals across Creation. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">3. His Glorious Majesty Emperor Genivam The 99th - Fair Folk Noble, leader of the Opal Court. Links to Raksha. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">4. Dead Kofi - Ghost and bureacrat in the Sijan Mortician\u2019s Guild. Underworld connections. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">5. Awareness of Vacuity - 2nd-circle demon Wei smuggled out of Yu-Shan and back into Malfeas. Links to major players in Hell. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Artifact ****:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Handy Sack: A useful toy, thought to once have been Mercury's own traveling bag, now passed around the members of the Golden Barque who are planning to go on long expeditions and do not know exactly what they should bring along.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The handy sack is a large brown grain sack that always appears to be partly full of something soft and lumpy. Anyone who looks inside it will only see darkness. Once per scene, the bearer of the sack can spend one mote and pull out any object from the sack that has a Resources cost of one dot or less. Alternately, the bearer can commit one mote to put something into the sack (provided that it is small enough to fit), for later retrieval. Neither adding nor removing objects from the sack affects its weight.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The sack cannot be used without spending motes. Persons reaching into the sack will not grab hold of anything, and items put into the sack will fall out of the bottom, despite there being no obvious hole.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">If the sack is turned over, a small amount of dried grain (randomly rice, millet, barley, or wheat) will pour out onto the ground. If this happens, the sack will appear empty, and cannot be used again for one full day. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Backing *</span></span></span> (Golden Barque - Eastern Direction - Convention on Fair Folk - Independent)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Colleges:</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Resplendent Destiny: The Gull ***</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Resplendent Destiny: The Ship\u2019s Wheel **</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Resplendent Destiny: The Rising Smoke **</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Stat Block</span></b></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Wei begins play with no weapons or armor - just the clothes on his back and the Handy Sack.</span></span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Combat Block</span></b></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Personal: 12</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Peripheral: 33</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">?/? WP 6/6</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">DDV: 5</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">PDV: 2</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">MDV: 4</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Soak:</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">0A/XL/XB Natural</span></span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Hardness: 0</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Move:</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">3/6 Normal</span></span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Jump:</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">4v/8h normal</span></span></span></li> </ul></li> </ul> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 07-01-2014, 09:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T16:30:24-07:00","id":185195,"title":"","content":"Wait, are we playing with the houserule where you get free ox-body purchases equal to your stamina? I've seen people do that every now and then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","name":"4uk4ata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T00:46:19-07:00","id":185405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>4uk4ata</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/180713-ooc-should-the-sun-not-rise-sidereals-2-5?p=185195#post185195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, are we playing with the houserule where you get free ox-body purchases equal to your stamina? I've seen people do that every now and then.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, we are not. And as such, semicasual, Lucky Wei's Health Levels are off.<br /> <br /> You're also entitled to four free Specialties as per the 2.5 character generation rules, which you haven't taken. <br /> <br /> Finally, there are a few issues with his Backgrounds.<br /> - Savant isn't a Background we'll be using in this game. (Backgrounds are supposed to reflect a character's connection to the setting and/or provide plot hooks to go with their benefits, but Savant is wholly internal and only provides bonus dice, the last thing the game needs more sources of. So I think it's a bad Background. Instead, I recommend Lore and Occult specialties in &quot;the First Age&quot;.)<br /> - You don't have any Backing or Salary. Even the most junior members of the Fellowship have at least Salary 1 unless something extraordinary is going on, so if you don't want to take that, please provide a reason in your backstory for why Wei's funding has been cut off. Likewise, &quot;members in good standing of the Bureau have at least Backing 1 from their Maiden's Division and from one of the Directional Conventions.&quot; As is, Lucky Wei very nearly looks like a Ronin.<br /> - Not an issue, but just to verify that you've seen it: I commented on your Allies in a PM last week. <br /> <br /> Other than that, the sheet looks good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2082-schleiermacher","name":"Schleiermacher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T05:53:55-07:00","id":185454,"title":"","content":"I changed the health levels to the standard 7, plus 2 Dying for my stamina. I'm not sure where I got the notion of 5x0, 3x-1.<br /> <br /> I put my specialty dots into more folk hero archetypal things.<br /> <br /> Replaced Savant * with Backing * - Wei is at least tolerated as a member of his department.<br /> <br /> I didn't give Wei a salary mostly because it doesn't fit the archetype for someone like him to have the kind of money even Salary * would allow. If you want an in-character reason, I propose that Wei's salary is being withheld as punishment for him not doing his job properly - Wei will take any excuse he can to go out and do field work, but getting him to do paperwork practically requires a senior member of the Golden Barque to be watching him at all times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T14:52:25-07:00","id":185805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/180713-ooc-should-the-sun-not-rise-sidereals-2-5?p=185454#post185454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Replaced Savant * with Backing * - Wei is at least tolerated as a member of his department.<br /> <br /> I didn't give Wei a salary mostly because it doesn't fit the archetype for someone like him to have the kind of money even Salary * would allow. If you want an in-character reason, I propose that Wei's salary is being withheld as punishment for him not doing his job properly - Wei will take any excuse he can to go out and do field work, but getting him to do paperwork practically requires a senior member of the Golden Barque to be watching him at all times.</div> </di